  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Agriculture and LIvestock Value chain Enhancement (ALIVE)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;General Objective: To strengthen resilience to recurrent emergencies and improve access to basic services for vulnerable groups. Specific Objective: To improve the drinking water and sanitation conditions of IDPs, refugees, migrants, host communities and people affected by natural disasters in North Darfur.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The project will target vulnerable communities particularly at risk of epidemics/floods in the Kabkabya area (North Darfur) and integrates with an ongoing action financed by the Sudan Humanitarian Fund in the same area always in the Water, Hygiene and Shelter sector. Results: Water supply and sanitation conditions are improved for the displaced population and the resident population of Kabkabiya; Knowledge of proper practices of drinking water use and consumption is improved among the communities residing in the Kabkabiya area; Increased knowledge of proper sanitation practices in rural settings and implementation of family latrines resulting in abandonment of the practice of open defecation.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
